35,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found out that some people in the coordination group are doing a lot of work by hand. It seems very tiring for them.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I discovered that network coverage at customer plants is quite unstable, and getting device approval takes far too long.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The budget is a mess. We have room in the software allowance, but the capital budget is frozen. We must avoid per-head licences.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"It's just as I feared. The big, fancy projects that required everyone to participate just died. Only the small, specific tools survived.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found that we are losing an hour every day just copying records, and we have delivery errors because different units use different addresses.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Midori, that sounds so sad. Copying things for an hour must be very boring. I wish we could help them.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@May, your finding about the failed rollouts aligns with my discovery. If the groundwork is unstable, the project cannot survive.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, that is exactly why we cannot commit to a project that requires a large capital outlay or expensive recurring licences.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly! So why do we keep proposing these ""grand visions"" that just vanish after a year? We need something practical.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"I agree. If we could just fix the address lists and the copying problem, it would save so much time and stress.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I also saw that the developers are very busy. If we pick a project, will it just make the coordination group even more tired?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If we ignore the external conditions, like the network issues I found, we are simply setting the developers up for failure.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,I am concerned that we will agree to a project today and then find out next year that we cannot afford the renewal fees.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"Let's stop dreaming about the ""perfect"" system. We need a tool that actually stays in use, not a trophy for the board.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I feel like we are all seeing the same thing. The ""big"" ideas are failing, while the people on the floor are struggling with simple things.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I want to support the people who are working hard. I hope the candidates are projects that help them.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for whatever seems most realistic and least likely to be disrupted by things we cannot control.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,I will be looking for a project that fits within the current software allowance and avoids long-term financial traps.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"I'll be the judge of whether these candidates are just more of the same ""grand visions"" or something that will actually last.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,I'll look for the one that addresses those everyday losses we've been talking about.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
