60,3,1,talk,Minato,,Candidate A sounds like it would help the people in the coordination group who are writing everything by hand. I like that.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Candidate D seems risky. I found that network coverage at customer plants is poor and device approval is slow. It might fail.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,Candidate C is a simple data consolidation. It likely requires minimal capital and avoids the per-head licence traps of a complex app.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Candidate A is exactly the kind of ""shared tool"" that usually dies because it requires everyone to use it. Candidate C is a record, which lasts.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,Candidate C is perfect. It solves the misrouted deliveries caused by different addresses and stops the need to copy records between units.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, do you think Candidate A is too hard? I just thought it would make the people less tired.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with May. Candidate A depends on everyone's participation. Candidate C is a foundation. It is more serene.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,Candidate C is the only one that doesn't look like a financial time bomb. It is a one-time effort to clean the data.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"See? Even George is on board. Candidate C is a boring, practical tool. Boring is good. Boring survives.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,I'm so glad we're agreeing. Candidate C directly addresses the everyday losses I found in the logs.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"If everyone likes Candidate C, then I am happy too. I want everyone to be peaceful and not too stressed.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,It is the most stable choice. It does not rely on the unpredictable network conditions of other companies' premises.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,It is the only responsible choice given the frozen capital budget. We can handle this within our current means.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"It's a win for the ""boring"" side of the house. I'll take it over another failed ""innovation"" any day.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,It's wonderful that we're looking at the actual problems on the floor instead of just what sounds impressive.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,I've learned a lot today. I think I'm ready to vote for Candidate C.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am also ready. Candidate C is the most grounded option.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,I have seen enough. Candidate C is the only one that makes financial sense.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm sold. Let's go with the one that actually has a chance of being used in two years.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,I feel very relieved. I'm happy to vote for Candidate C.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
